              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "necessitās, necessitātis — \"necessity, need; compulsion\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Necessitās mē coēgit. Necessity forced me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "necessitās, necessitātis f., the noun of necesse, needful. Necessitās nōn habet lēgem, necessity knows no law. English necessity."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "necessitās is built on necesse \"needful\" (Lewis & Short), which EtymDB takes as ne- \"not\" with cessus, from cēdō \"to give way\": what does not give way. English necessity comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
