              "text": "opportūnus, opportūna, opportūnum — \"convenient, timely, opportune\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Tempus opportūnum exspectāmus. We are waiting for a convenient time."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "opportūnus, opportūna, opportūnum: said first of a wind blowing towards the harbour, then of anything well timed. English opportune."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "opportūnus is built from ob \"towards\" and portus \"a harbour\" (Lewis & Short): of a wind that drives you into port. English opportune and opportunity come from it."
            }
          ]
        },
